{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Afterward caught in a thicket.</b> Afterward he saw the ram caught in the thicket of the forest. And similarly its antecedent: 'after the instrumentalists' — afterward came the instrumentalists; 'and the clouds returned after the rain' — afterward came the rain. And he saw it as it was caught, as Rashi explained; then Abraham understood that it was placed there by HaShem. But had it been standing nearby like other rams, Abraham might have thought that perhaps it belonged to others, and he would have lost it through them. Another interpretation: <b>afterward</b> it was <b>caught — by its horns</b> — in the thicket of the forest."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase 'וכן קדמו שרים אחר נוגנים' likely references a verse or idiom; rendered hyper-literally as the reference is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:19.107669708Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}